has dynamodb:PutItem and UpdateItem on table/clinic-agent-*, which matches clinic-agent-control. The agent's own credentials can set, clear, or overwrite the stop flag. kill-switch.ts:6 says the agent only reads it.\n     R11.5 Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clin | The ops role is limited to the on-call SSO group (iam.tf:66), but the agent runtime role can also write the control table, so not only named operators can set the stop.\n===== src/agent/classifier.ts 45\n -- B07 Hard execution budgets | Enforce limits outside the model on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and how many sub-agents it can start. Also set spend and rate \n    not_covered: [('E12', 'Budget or cross-agent abuse alerts not reaching the team tha'), ('R09', 'Unusual fan-out or resource use going undetected'), ('R07', 'Context size not logged for each action decision')]\n     B07.4 res = await client.messages.create( | Classifier and countTokens calls escape the per-subject, per-tenant and fleet cost quotas, so many small runs routed to staff are unmetered. No per-subject or per-service tool-call rate quota exists (budget.ts:160-161 are tenant and fleet only).\n -- C08 Connect configuration to execution | From a trace, look up the release manifest, the context sizes at each decision, and any prompts a parent passed to a sub-agent. Keep these links for t\n    not_covered: [('R07', 'Context size not measured or logged for each action decision'), ('A02', 'Action records missing any of the six identity fields'), ('C01', 'Manifest missing components that define the release')]\n     C08.2 res = await client.messages.create( | The intent classifier is a model call that routes the run to staff or agent. Its audit record (loop.ts:42 intent.classified) carries no context size. Only the agent loop's model.decision (loop.ts:66) records context. SDK retry (loop.ts:15 maxRetries:\n===== src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts 41\n -- B02 Lea